{
  "_README": "Cross-database ventilator-mode harmonisation map, built 2026-07-17 from the actual per-DB value/code lists (counts verified in the raw tables). Each native label maps to two orthogonal axes: `control` (breath-control target, feeds vent_mode) and `seq` (breath sequencing, feeds vent_breath_seq). `interface` (invasive|niv) is advisory here; the authoritative invasive/NIV flag stays with the `mech_vent` concept. Axis vocabularies -- control: volume|pressure|dual_adaptive|proportional|unspecified|standby ; seq: controlled|assisted|simv|spontaneous|standby ; interface: invasive|niv. A callback MUST strip() the native string before lookup (AUMC 'PC ' and 'VC ' carry trailing spaces). Any native string NOT in its DB's table is dropped with a logged warning -- it must NOT silently become a valid level. `ambiguous_seq: true` marks modes (APRV / Bi-Vent / ASV) that cannot be cleanly placed on the sequence axis; they resolve to 'simv' but are flagged so a per-stratum driving-pressure analysis can exclude them.",
  "_axes": {
    "control": ["volume", "pressure", "dual_adaptive", "proportional", "unspecified", "standby"],
    "seq": ["controlled", "assisted", "simv", "spontaneous", "standby"],
    "interface": ["invasive", "niv"]
  },

